---
import InstructionNote from '../InstructionNote.astro';
---
<section id="ux-content">
    <h2>UX & Content Design</h2>
    

    <h3>Visual UI States</h3>

    <h4>Text Links</h4>
    <p>Links must be distinguishable by more than just color. <strong>Default:</strong> Underlined.</p>
    <div style="padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
        <p style="margin: 0;">This is a paragraph containing a <a href="#" style="text-decoration: underline; color: inherit;"><strong>text link</strong></a> to demonstrate the default state.</p>
    </div>

    <h4>Button States</h4>
    <p>Buttons must have a highly visible focus indicator (e.g., outline) for keyboard navigation.</p>
    <div style="padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
        <button style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; font-size: 1rem; background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #333333; outline: 3px solid #000000; outline-offset: 2px;">Focused Button</button>
    </div>

    <h4>Touch Targets</h4>
    <p>Interactive elements must have a target size of at least 44x44 CSS pixels to accommodate touch inputs.</p>
    <div style="padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
        <div style="width: 44px; height: 44px; background-color: #333333; color: #ffffff; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.75rem;">44px</div>
    </div>

    <h3>Structure & Semantics</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Form Labels:</strong> All form inputs must include persistent, visible labels that clearly describe the information being requested. Labels must appear outside the input field and remain visible at all times. Additionally, required fields must be clearly indicated using text and symbols.</li>
        <li><strong>Heading Structure:</strong> Headings organize content into a clear hierarchy that improves readability and navigation. Assistive technologies utilize headings to help users quickly scan and jump between sections of a page. Splitli follows a consistent heading structure using semantic HTML tags. Our guidelines include headings following a logical order without skipping levels, each page including one H1 heading that represents the main topic of the page, major sections using H2 headings, and subsections using H3 headings.</li>
    </ul>
</section>